Having a "snapshot" save feature _is_ a good idea (i.e. not requiring
that you end the game and restart). However, this will require major
changes in the way things work before it gets implemented. For now,
the best recourse is to save early and often. You could also use a
script to run the game and the script could copy the save directory
to a backup directory just before starting the game (perhaps with
additional logic). This also provides some measure of protection,
if you can afford the space.

Now about the game's stability status ... hmmmm.

